  "solution": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> be the thermal capacity of the calorimeter and specific heat of water = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>kg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.<br />Heat lost by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> of water = Heat gained by water in calorimeter + Heat gained by calorimeter<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8658;&#160;</mo>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160; </mrow> </math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>X</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8658;</mo> </mrow> </math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1260</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#1